# Metrics 2.5.1 shadow tooling regenerates these docs deterministically with LF
# (scripts write with newline="\n" so report/canonical hashes stay byte-stable
# across platforms). Under core.autocrlf=true git would otherwise expect CRLF on
# checkout and flag a re-generated LF file as "modified" even though the committed
# blob is byte-identical — a phantom change that dirties the worktree during
# verification. Pin these exact generated paths to LF so re-running the generators
# is churn-free.
docs/metrics-2.5.1-rollout-gate.json text eol=lf
docs/metrics-2.5.1-rollout-gate.md   text eol=lf
docs/metrics-2.5.1-baseline.json     text eol=lf
docs/metrics-2.5.1-baseline.md       text eol=lf
